      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4652022::webcard",
        "PMC7514121::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A V-containing refractory alloy can form a disordered BCC structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4652022::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preserving the BCC solid solution would preserve the relevant dislocation-based strengthening mechanisms.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitation-related strengthening contributes to the strength of the proposed alloy and would be preserved by Hf-to-V substitution.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium is significantly lighter than hafnium.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Hf with V will lower alloy density by reducing the alloy's average atomic mass.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium's similar valence and refractory nature will maintain dislocation mobility and slip-system interactions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
